within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.C_CardiovascularSystem.C09A_AceInhibitorsPlain.C09AA01_Captopril;
model Captopril_Kiriyama2024_PD_bp
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Kiriyama_2024 :: BP (blood pressure)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 105,      // [mmHg]
    Emax = -41.8,  // [mmHg]
    EC50 = 0.007885,  // [kg/m3; ng/mL × 1e-06]
    gamma = 0.662,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng/mL per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 79000, Interval = 158),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Captopril_Kiriyama2024_PD_bp</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Kiriyama A et al., <i>Pharmacology research &amp; perspectives 12(4):e1249</i> 2024 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/prp2.1249\">doi:10.1002/prp2.1249</a>) — blood pressure [mmHg] against captopril ng/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =        105 mmHg     drug-free response (baseline) (E0, Q324)
  Emax  =       41.8 mmHg     maximal effect term (Emax, Q323)
  EC50  =       7885 ng/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50, Q321)
  gamma =      0.662          Hill coefficient (γ, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng/mL of captopril per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 105   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (7885 ng/mL)  response 84.1
  exposure -> infinity  response 63.2</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Kiriyama_2024: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Captopril_Kiriyama2024_PD_bp;
